    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L10-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Imaginary Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Sometimes people call the number line the real number line.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L10-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Imaginary Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "All real numbers are either positive, negative, or 0, and they can be plotted on this line. All the numbers we have used until this lesson have been real numbers. For real numbers, we know that:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L10-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Imaginary Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A positive number times a positive number is always positive. So when we square a positive number, the result will always be positive.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L10-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Imaginary Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A negative number times a negative number is always positive. So when we square a negative number, the result will always be positive.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L10-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Imaginary Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "So squaring a real number never results in a negative number. We can conclude that the equation \\(x^2 = \\text{-} 1\\) does not have any real number solutions. In other words, none of the numbers on the real number line satisfy this…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L10-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Imaginary Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Mathematicians invented a new number that is not on the real number line. This new number was invented as a solution to the equation \\(x^2 = \\text{-} 1\\). For now, let’s write it \\(\\sqrt{\\text- 1}\\) and draw a point to represent this…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L10-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Imaginary Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "This new number \\(\\sqrt{\\text- 1}\\) is a solution to the equation \\(x^2 = \\text{-} 1\\), so \\(\\left(\\sqrt{\\text- 1}\\right)^2 = \\text-1\\). If we draw a line that passes through 0 on the real number line and \\(\\sqrt{\\text- 1}\\), we get the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L10-ACTIVITY-025",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Imaginary Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A number on the imaginary number line. It can be written as \\(bi\\), where \\(b\\) is a real number and \\(i^2 = \\text-1\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
